<title>USA: U.S. stocks open down.</title>
<headline>U.S. stocks open down.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. stocks opened down on Tuesday with Wall Street taking some profits after Monday's record close at 6,567 points.</p>
<p>Investors were likely to be watching economic indicators, especially factory orders released at 1500 GMT for signs of quicker economic growth.</p>
<p>Dow Industrials were off seven to 6561 points. The Nasdaq Composite was down 0.44 to 1315.96.</p>
